name:Dominus vobiscum. Oremus. Exaudi nos (after the Asperges);
office-part:Oratio;
book:Missale O.P. (1939), p. 33, text and punctuation; set to the Dominican tone of the prayers "quae non sunt de corpore Officii et Missae", Processionarium O.P. (1913), pp. 407-408 (Art. III, III): Dominus vobiscum and Oremus (1°), metrum at ":" and flexa at ";" (2°), the short conclusion and Amen (3°);
transcriber:set to the printed tone (F clef on the 3rd line, reciting note h);
